1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,640
Your rival can see your NFT.
But can they read its strength before a fight?

2
00:00:04,898 --> 00:00:09,650
In Ashenkin, a creature exists onchain
while its hidden genes stay encrypted.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:16,152
Sign in with a wallet or email.
Your identity restores a Circle-managed game wallet.

4
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:24,247
Need gas? The funded daily faucet offers
0.002 Sepolia ETH per account, every 24 hours.

5
00:00:24,397 --> 00:00:29,650
Mint an NFT before playing. Circle handles
hosted signing; blockchain actions still use gas.

6
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:35,504
Appearance and ownership are public.
Hidden alleles contribute to a Xeno’s real power.

7
00:00:35,961 --> 00:00:41,385
Breeding passes traits through encrypted
inheritance and Zama-generated randomness.

8
00:00:41,842 --> 00:00:47,650
Owners choose which genes to sequence privately,
or deliberately make the full genome public.

9
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:56,624
This optional practice uses local rolls.
It requires an NFT, but gives no rewards and uses no gas.

10
00:00:57,909 --> 00:01:04,053
First, the rival’s moves are concealed.
Now expose the same plan and keep the same rolls.

11
00:01:05,338 --> 00:01:11,650
You can choose a counter for every exposed move.
That is why the real match keeps plans encrypted.

12
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:17,264
This is a replay of Wild Hunt number one,
a completed match on Ethereum Sepolia.

13
00:01:17,797 --> 00:01:25,189
Zama generates hidden rolls for each fighter.
FHE scores moves and private strength together.

14
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:31,650
The challenger won rounds one and two,
then lost round three. Two rounds secured the capture.

15
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:37,696
Anyone can open the fight log
and choose Verify the rounds, without signing in.

16
00:01:40,837 --> 00:01:48,613
The app requests all three public KMS results
and compares them with the settled Sepolia record.

17
00:01:51,754 --> 00:01:59,650
The original settlement checked the KMS proof onchain.
Checking it again needs no new transaction.

18
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:06,320
Your Xeno can also face a daily challenge
while you are offline, within the sponsor budget.

19
00:02:06,473 --> 00:02:14,129
Zama randomizes the encounter, difficulty and loot.
FHE checks hidden strength, element and luck.

20
00:02:14,282 --> 00:02:21,698
A verified win adds items to its field bag.
If it fails, there is no reward and nothing is lost.

21
00:02:21,851 --> 00:02:29,651
The server pays for the trial and checks its proof.
The owner signs no claim. Here, Verify repeats the check.

22
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:35,864
The first Trail lantern needs three Ash thread,
or one thread and one Archive fragment.

23
00:02:36,265 --> 00:02:42,745
Choose a recipe when your bag has enough materials.
Crafting is free of gas and grants a cosmetic.

24
00:02:43,146 --> 00:02:49,650
These are server-managed game items, not token yield.
The lantern gives no combat bonus or guaranteed wins.

25
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:54,909
Visit Ashenkin dot X Y Z.
Sign in, mint a Xeno and explore its world.

26
00:02:55,059 --> 00:02:59,650
Play the game. Verify the result.
The source is on GitHub: duclucky slash ashenkin.
